{
  "schema": 1,
  "comment": "The owner checks of kit. A changed module of scripts/kit or tests/kit runs typecheck, duplication-check and lint-ts, the TypeScript lint that kit gives its consumers (K142), and the tests of tests/kit that import it, directly or through other modules, as the import graph of owner-check finds them (K191); a file of scripts/kit or tests/kit that is no module, such as a schema, a fixture or kit.mk, runs the tests that import the modules that read it. kit-test, the whole tool suite, is CI's full run and no owner. The package files run the checks that read them. The real tool tests of tests/source wait for the full run unless an explicit owner rule selects them. A changed tests/source test runs itself. consumer-layout and fresh-checkout verify installation and package consumption in a sandbox without rerunning a test suite, so they run only for themselves and their helper tests/source/checkout.mts. LICENSE and .editorconfig, which an editor reads, are read by no check.",
  "ciExempt": [
    { "target": "hooks-check", "reason": "needs the local core.hooksPath that make install-hooks writes; a CI checkout has no hooks to check" }
  ],
